  "description": "Aggregate top-K routed expert outputs using normalized routing gate probabilities.\n\nMixture of Experts routes tokens conditionally to specialized subnetworks, increasing total parameter capacity by orders of magnitude at constant compute budget.\n\n### Mathematical Formulation\n$$\n\\mathbf{y}_t = \\sum_{i=1}^K g_{t, i} \\mathbf{E}_{t, i}(\\mathbf{x}_t)\n$$\n\n### Step-by-Step Implementation\n1. Multiply each expert output vector by its corresponding gating coefficient g\n2. Sum scaled vectors across top-k active experts per token\n3. Return aggregated token representations rounded to 4 decimal places\n\n### Returns\nNested 2D list of shape (N, D) representing aggregated MoE layer activations.",
  "theory": "## Understanding the Theory: Implement MoE Token Dispatch and Expert Aggregation\n\n### Core Intuition: Why Do We Need This?\nNatural language consists of discrete words and symbols arranged in sequential order. To process text with neural networks, we convert words into continuous embedding vectors and model their grammatical and semantic relationships. **Implement MoE Token Dispatch and Expert Aggregation** is a core sequence-processing mechanism used in modern Transformer and LLM architectures.\n\nMixture of Experts routes tokens conditionally to specialized subnetworks, increasing total parameter capacity by orders of magnitude at constant compute budget. In this problem, the goal is to: aggregate top-k routed expert outputs using normalized routing gate probabilities.\n\n### Mathematical Principles & Formulation\nThe core governing equation for this operation is:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{y}_t = \\sum_{i=1}^K g_{t, i} \\mathbf{E}_{t, i}(\\mathbf{x}_t)\n$$\n\nEvery term in this formulation plays a precise mathematical role in ensuring dimensional consistency, numerical stability, and correct algorithmic behavior.\n\n### Step-by-Step Computational Workflow\n1. **Phase 1**: Multiply each expert output vector by its corresponding gating coefficient g\n2. **Phase 2**: Sum scaled vectors across top-k active experts per token\n3. **Phase 3**: Return aggregated token representations rounded to 4 decimal places\n\n### Practical Machine Learning Applications & Nuances\n* **Self-Attention Mechanics**: Scaled dot-product attention computes all-to-all token interactions dynamically, allowing tokens to gather context from the entire sentence simultaneously.\n* **Position Encodings**: Because self-attention is permutation-invariant, positional encodings (like sinusoidal or Rotary Position Embeddings) inject word order into the representations.\n* **Vocabulary & Subwords**: Algorithms like BPE tokenize text into frequent subwords, allowing models to represent rare words without requiring an infinite vocabulary.",
